# Vercel Web Analytics Configuration Report

## Summary
Verified and confirmed that Vercel Web Analytics is **already properly installed and configured** in this Next.js project.

## Current Implementation Status

### 1. Package Installation ✅
- Package: `@vercel/analytics` version 2.0.1 (latest)
- Already listed in `package.json` dependencies
- Successfully installed via `npm install`

### 2. Analytics Component Configuration ✅
- **File**: `bluprynt/app/layout.tsx`
- **Implementation**: Analytics component from `@vercel/analytics/next` is imported and placed correctly
- **Location**: Component is positioned at the end of the `<body>` tag, following Next.js App Router best practices

### Code Verification
The root layout file includes:
```typescript
import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next";

export default async function RootLayout({ children }: { children: React.ReactNode }) {
  return (
    <html>
      <body>
        <SheetProvider>
          {!isAdminRoute && <CADCrosshair />}
          {!isAdminRoute && <CADNavbar />}
          {children}
        </SheetProvider>
        <Analytics />  
      </body>
    </html>
  );
}
```

## Implementation Details

### Framework Detected
- **Framework**: Next.js 15.0.0 with App Router
- **Configuration Method**: Added `<Analytics />` component to root layout

### Documentation Reference
Followed the official Vercel Analytics quickstart guide from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart
- Used Next.js App Router specific instructions
- Import from `@vercel/analytics/next`
- Component placed at end of body tag

## Changes Made
- **Modified Files**: 
  - `package-lock.json` - Updated lockfile after running `npm install` to ensure dependencies are properly resolved

- **No Code Changes Required**: The Analytics component was already properly configured in the codebase

